---
description: Medical-safety guardrails for any code touching model output or user-facing copy
globs: ["backend/**/*.py", "web/**/*"]
alwaysApply: false
---
- Model output is untrusted. Only `text` and `candidates` (list of strings) may leave the OCR layer.
- Candidates must appear in the extracted text (see `sanitize_candidates`). Do not loosen this.
- UI/API copy must not say "switch", "replace", "safe", "recommended", or "correct" about a medicine match.
- Non-exact fuzzy matches always carry a "please verify" notice. Uncertain matches show no price.
- Every OCR/prescription response includes `disclaimer` (single source: `backend/app/disclaimer.py`).
